speechtext:
The
President of the Privy Council (Mr. Macdonald) moves:
That when Bill C-215, an act respecting the franchise of electors and the election of members to the House of Commons, is being considered in committee of the whole, only such clauses, and other provisions, or parts thereof, that propose the

Proceedings on Adjournment Motion enactment of new or amended provisions in relation to the Canada Elections Act and which are indicated by vertical rules shall be open for consideration and amendment;
That all other clauses and other provisions, or parts thereof, when called from the Chair shall be deemed to have been adopted without amendment or debate;
Provided that any clause, subclause or other provision referred to in paragraph two above, may be brought under consideration or reconsideration by any members who rises and proposes a motion to amend any such clause, subclause or other provision of the bill that may be accepted by the Chair.
